  "title": "Clean Kit Barcode and Extract Components",
  "prompt": "The `kit_shipments` table stores diagnostic test kits with a `raw_barcode` column that contains a barcode string in the format `KIT-<region>-<batch>-<sequence>`, but the data has inconsistent casing, leading/trailing spaces, and sometimes extra internal spaces. Write a query that returns each kit with: (1) `kit_id`, (2) `cleaned_barcode` (trimmed, uppercase), (3) `region_code` (the second segment after the first dash), (4) `batch_number` (the third segment), and (5) `sequence_number` (the fourth segment). Order results by `kit_id` ascending. The barcode format is always four dash-separated parts, but whitespace and case vary.",
