  "hints": [
    "Start by trimming and converting the entire barcode to uppercase to normalize the data.",
    "Use SPLIT_PART with a dash delimiter to extract specific segments; the function is 1-based, so the region is segment 2.",
    "Chain the UPPER and BTRIM functions around the raw_barcode, then apply SPLIT_PART to the cleaned string for each component."
  ],
  "answer_key": "SELECT\n  kit_id,\n  UPPER(BTRIM(raw_barcode)) AS cleaned_barcode,\n  SPLIT_PART(UPPER(BTRIM(raw_barcode)), '-', 2) AS region_code,\n  SPLIT_PART(UPPER(BTRIM(raw_barcode)), '-', 3) AS batch_number,\n  SPLIT_PART(UPPER(BTRIM(raw_barcode)), '-', 4) AS sequence_number\nFROM kit_shipments\nORDER BY kit_id;",
